  "notes": [
    "Code-verified against routes/Agents.svelte, components/agents/AgentsOverview.svelte, components/agents/create/CreateAgent.svelte, CreateAgentDraft.svelte, CreateAgentReview.svelte, agentDraft.ts and components/agents/sheet/AdjustAccess.svelte.",
    "No model answers in a deterministic book, so the draft is not written by a model: send_chat_message is stubbed, and get_chat_session is patched with a conversation whose last answer carries a propose_agent call. The patched messages imitate ChatMessageView and ToolCallView of crates/apollia-desktop/src/commands/chat.rs, and the output of the call imitates AgentDraftResult and AgentDraft of crates/apollia-runtime/src/chat/agent_draft_tool.rs: a field renamed there drifts here silently. The real tool, the real offer and the real conversation are held by the runtime tests chat::agent_draft_tool and chat::manager::agent_draft_tests.",
    "The patch on get_chat_session is cleared by the last step and is never armed across a model turn: the book plays none.",
    "create_agent_definition is stubbed, refused once then accepted, so the book writes no agent into the seeded home; its answer and the one of get_agent_definition imitate ResolvedAgentResponse of crates/apollia-runtime/src/api/routes_agent_definitions.rs. The real creation is held by the runtime tests api::routes_agent_definitions::tests_create.",
    "The session of the second pass is a real one, created by the seeded runtime and deleted when the screen is left. The accesses of the draft, web_search and file_write, are tools of the seeded registry, described by the real describe_tool.",
    "agent-create-try is observed, not clicked: it opens a conversation with an agent the stub did not store. The grant dialogs of the form are played by agents-det on the sheet of an existing agent.",
    "Not folded into master-det: this book has not been through a runtime round yet. Add it to ORDER in tools/regen_master.py after its first green solo run: just automation-seeded scripts/automation/agent-create-det.json"
  ]
}
